@page "/"

<PageTitle>Yarn Shaper</PageTitle>

<div class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Garment shaping calculator</span>
    <h1>Turn gauge and measurements into a knitting schedule you can actually see.</h1>
    <p>
        Yarn Shaper computes garment shaping — raglan sweater increases, and
        more constructions to come — from your gauge and finished
        measurements, then renders the resulting stitch and row geometry
        live as an SVG schematic. No generic mockup: the diagram is drawn
        directly from the same numbers a knitter would follow.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="raglan">Try the raglan calculator</a>
        <a class="btn-link" href="https://github.com/mollygilchrist03/YarnShaper" target="_blank">View source</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="card feature-card">
        <span class="badge badge-ready">Available now</span>
        <h3>Raglan yoke shaping</h3>
        <p>Back, front, and both sleeves, shaped round by round from neck cast-on to underarm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card feature-card">
        <span class="badge badge-soon">Coming soon</span>
        <h3>Sock heel turns</h3>
        <p>Heel turn and gusset pickup math, rendered with the same schematic renderer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card feature-card">
        <span class="badge badge-soon">Coming soon</span>
        <h3>Granny square rounds</h3>
        <p>Round-by-round geometry — another natural fit for the colorway layer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card feature-card">
        <span class="badge badge-ready">Available now</span>
        <h3>Colorway preview</h3>
        <p>Map a stripe sequence onto the real construction — every section recolors in sync, round by round.</p>
    </div>
</div>
